    "body": "# What does this PR do?\n\nFixes #10887.\n\n`_preprocess_image` called `convert(\"RGB\")` on RGBA, LA and transparent-palette images, which dropped the alpha channel without a background, so transparent pixels came out black and black lines on them vanished. It now composites such images onto a white background first. The API server in `api/chat.py` no longer converts to RGB as soon as it opens an image (it calls `load()` instead, so the stream is still read right away), so the same handling applies to images sent there. White matches what vLLM and lmms-eval do for transparency.\n\nThe new tests cover RGBA, LA and transparent-palette PNGs and fail on main at the background pixel (0 != 255). `tests/data/test_mm_plugin.py`: 18 passed, 2 skipped.\n\nThis fix was written with an AI coding agent pipeline and reviewed before I opened this PR.\n\n## Before submitting\n\n- [x] Did you read the [contributor guideline](https://github.com/hiyouga/LLaMA-Factory/blob/main/.github/CONTRIBUTING.md)?\n- [x] Did you write any new necessary tests?\n",
